failures.answer:
The applicable chest‑deflection limit depends on the dummy percentile and the test speed. For a Hybrid III dummy the limits are: 
• 5 % percentile – < 18 mm at 35/50 km/h, < 22 mm at 56 km/h; 
• 50 % percentile – 20 mm (lower‑performance limit) and 42 mm (upper‑performance limit) at 35/50 km/h, 42 mm at 56 km/h; 
• 95 % percentile – < 28 mm (lower‑performance limit) and 55 mm (upper‑performance limit) at 35/50 km/h, 55 mm at 56 km/h. 
These values are the chest‑deflection limits that must be met in a frontal impact test with a Hybrid III dummy.

